        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After embarrassingly long time of debugging, the issue was that `ui_select()` called `on_choice(item, idx)` with `item` being a copy of original `items[idx]`. This is not *exactly* prohibited and overall relying in `on_choice()` that the item is exact one is not a good approach.\r\n\r\nThis should now be fixed on `main`. But I've also made a akinsho/toggleterm.nvim#566 PR to address this for other `ui.select()` implementations.",
